          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page No- 143-44"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.561,
            0.3,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it out",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.582,
            0.925,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A light bulb is ON. Dorjee toggles its switch 77 times. Will the bulb be on or off? Why?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.624,
            0.377,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The bulb will be OFF."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.666,
            0.926,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Liswini has a large old encyclopaedia. When she opened it, several loose pages fell out of it. She counted 50 sheets in total, each printed on both sides. Can the sum of the page numbers of the loose sheets be 6000? Why or why not?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.75,
            0.924,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Each sheet has two pages, one with an even number and the other with an odd number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.788,
            0.924,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since there are 50 sheets, so there will be fifty pages with an even number and 50 pages with an odd number"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.828,
            0.537,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sum of the even numbers is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "even",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.847,
            0.847,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sum of the odd numbers taken even number of times is also "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "even",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.867,
            0.925,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, 6000 being even, it is possible that sum of all the page numbers of the loose sheets could be 6000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
